{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour vector (in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"type":"text","text":" sides (left 0), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colours beside a triangle."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Coloring","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First fit in index order (the lexicographically first proper colouring of all) when it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already optimal. Otherwise each vertex in turn takes the least colour its prefix still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extends with (k-colouring’s self-reduction to its decision problem): a Kempe swap of the last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colouring found when one avoids the prefix, else DSatur branch and bound over the parts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after the prefix that the vertex touches (on sparse components with conflict-directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backjumping and restarts). Khuller and Vazirani show the lexicographically first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"four-colouring of a planar graph is NP-hard to find, though some four-colouring is found in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"polynomial time. It can be far slower than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":": on random sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"3-colourable graphs with 2n edges it took about 0.2 s at 1,000 vertices, 2.7 s at 2,000 and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over 100 s at 5,000, where "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" takes about a millisecond. The search does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"check for task cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/ExactColoring.swift#L659","fileName":"ExactColoring.swift"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE029lexicographicallyFirstMinimumC0AD0C0VyxGyF","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","text":"Coloring","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"ColoringModule"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/Coloring":{"abstract":[{"text":"A proper colouring of a graph’s vertices by the colours ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<colorCount"},{"text":", each of which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"used (unless preset colours skip some): the result of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"greedyColoring(order:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (JGraphT ","type":"text"},{"code":"VertexColoringAlgorithm.Coloring","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Graphs.jl ","type":"text"},{"code":"Coloring","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloring","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Coloring","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Coloring","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Coloring"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()":{"abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour vector (in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"text":" sides (left 0), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()"},{"text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours beside a triangle.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/document